# Contracts & Agreements — Structure & Conventions (READ FIRST)

_Root guide for the `04 - Contracts & Agreements` folder. Read this before adding or editing any agreement._

## The three areas

| Folder | What it holds |
|---|---|
| `00 - Customer agreement Templates` | Reusable templates for **enterprise / negotiated** deals, organised by motion (Microsoft Marketplace, Customer Cloud Hosting) + NDA + Tools. |
| `01 - Customer agreements (drafts and signed)` | **Executed** per-customer agreements (one folder per customer). Frozen records — never edited. |
| `02 - SaaS default agreements` | The **self-serve SaaS** product's default published set: Terms of Use, Privacy Policy, Cookie Policy, DPA, SLA. |

## How versioning works (snapshots)

- Every agreement lives inside a **dated snapshot folder**:
  - `YYYY-MM-DD - LATEST` = the active version
  - `YYYY-MM-DD - DRAFT` = work in progress
  - `YYYY-MM-DD` (bare date) = superseded history
- A new snapshot is cut when the **offer / agreements change materially** — not per customer, not per minor edit.
- **To change something:** duplicate the latest snapshot → rename to today's date → edit there. **Never edit a snapshot that has already been used in a signed agreement.**
- Exactly **one** `- LATEST` per folder. Each document's **in-doc effective date must match its folder date**.
- **Enterprise templates** snapshot the **whole package together** (Main Agreement + all attachments move as one). **SaaS components** are versioned **per document** (each its own folder), so they can change independently.
- SaaS and enterprise lineages are kept **separate** even when currently identical — they can diverge.

## Which documents apply where

| Document | How it's accepted | Self-serve SaaS | Enterprise – Marketplace | Enterprise – Hosting |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| *Governing commercial contract* | Accepted by org/user | Terms of Use (Product), click-accept | Order + Microsoft Standard Contract | Main Agreement + Attachment 1 |
| **Terms of Use (Product)** | Contract | ✅ it *is* the contract | ❌ MS Standard Contract governs | ❌ Main Agreement governs |
| **Privacy Policy** | User notice — *not* a contract term | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |
| **Cookie Policy** | User/browser consent — *not* a contract term | ✅ | ✅ | ✅ |
| **DPA** | Legal requirement (GDPR Art. 28) | ✅ click-through DPA | ✅ Marketplace DPA (14-day notice) | ✅ Attachment 3 hosting DPA (30-day notice) |
| **SLA** | Commercial promise — plan-dependent | ✅ eligible tiers (best-effort otherwise) | ✅ publisher SLA / Attachment 2 (99%) | ✅ Attachment 2 (99%) |

Notes:
- **Privacy & Cookie are accepted by individual users, not the enterprise org.** The Main Agreement's contract = Terms + SLA + DPA only; all personal-data processing is governed by the **DPA**. Privacy Policy = controller-side transparency notice; Cookie Policy = browser consent.
- The **DPA is legally required** wherever Normain processes personal data on a customer's behalf (incl. SaaS, as a click-through) — independent of price/plan. The **SLA is commercial** — included only on eligible/paid tiers.
- Privacy Policy – Website + Cookie Policy – Website apply to the marketing funnel and live in `04 - Marketing / 01 - Website`; the **Product** variants live here in `02 - SaaS default agreements`.

## The three DPAs

Each contract motion has its own DPA. They share **one standard subprocessor list** (drawn from the master *Pre-approved subprocessor list* in InfoSec / Vendor Management), differing only in the **hosting** subprocessors (Table 1):

| DPA | Used for | Table 1 — hosting subprocessors |
|---|---|---|
| **Marketplace DPA** (`00 / 01 - Microsoft Marketplace Template`) | Microsoft Marketplace deals — Normain-hosted, dedicated tenant | Azure, BetterStack, PostHog |
| **Customer Cloud Hosting DPA** (`00 / 02 - Customer Cloud Hosting Template`) | Customer self-hosts in their own cloud | BetterStack, PostHog (no Azure/AWS — customer's infra) |
| **SaaS DPA** (`02 - SaaS default agreements`) | Open self-serve SaaS (app.normain.com) | Azure, **AWS**, BetterStack, PostHog |

- **Table 2 (operations) is identical in all three** — the same set, incl. OpenAI and Anthropic.
- **AWS** appears only in the SaaS DPA (it hosts Anthropic's models there); excluded from the enterprise DPAs.
- **Sentry** is pre-approved but listed in no DPA (reserved for future use).
- Each DPA's subprocessor appendix is taken from the master Pre-approved subprocessor list; only Table 1 varies by deployment model.
